 "text": "In a world... where your Noster feed is wall-to-wall bots, reply guys, and \"free bitcoin giveaways\" from a guy named Satoshi Nakamoto Official Real... one relay dared to ask the question: \"Wait. Who invited you?\"\n\nThis fall... relay dot pleb dot one. The community Noster relay.\n\nBuilt on a hardened Rust core. Lightning fast. Censorship resistant. No trackers. Minimal logs. Basically, hack the planet... but politely.\n\nIts secret weapon? The Web of Trust. Nobody wanders in off the street. A member vouches for you, and every member gets five invites a month.\n\nInvite a spammer? You lose your invites for a month. Three strikes, and those invites are gone for good. But keep it clean for three months, and you're promoted to fifteen.\n\nSign in with your browser extension, or a remote signer. Your private key never leaves your device. Unlike E.T., it does not phone home.\n\nInside, members get the control surface: a live feed, a verified name at pleb dot one, and invites, ready to share.\n\nrelay dot pleb dot one. Quality... over quantity. Know a member? Get an invite. Don't? Request one, and a real human will take a look. Shall we play a game?",
